.SH NAME
lst \- list items in trash folders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    lst [OPTION...] [DIRECTORY]
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \fBlst\fR command lists files and/or directories which have been moved
to trash folders as defined by the freedesktop.org Trash
Specification <https://specifications.freedesktop.org/trash/latest>.
.PP
By default, output is limited to items removed from the current directory,
and is grouped by the day of deletion. Items are sorted by name (ascending)
followed by deletion time (descending).
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    $ lst
\&    [today]
\&    \-rw\-r\-\-r\-\-  1 409K May 23  2025 \*(AqMy account info.zip\*(Aq       [16:35]
\&
\&    [yesterday]
\&    \-rw\-r\-\-r\-\-  1 411K Apr 16 15:21 \*(AqPeek 2026\-04\-16 15\-21.gif\*(Aq [09:28]
\&    \-rw\-r\-\-r\-\-  1 411K Apr 16 15:19 \*(AqPeek 2026\-04\-16 15\-21.gif\*(Aq [07:19]
\&    drwxrwxr\-x  5 4.0K Dec 11  2025  perl5/                     [07:53]
.Ve
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`DIRECTORY\*(C'\fR argument can be used to limit the output to a different
location. This works even if the location itself was moved to the trash.
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    $ lst /some/deleted/dir
\&    [yesterday]
\&    \-rwxrwxr\-x  5 4.0K Dec 11  2025  my\-file                    [15:42]
.Ve
.SH OPTIONS
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP "\-\-all, \-a" 4
.IX Item "--all, -a"
Do not ignore items starting with a dot.
.IP "\-\-every\-directory, \-e" 4
.IX Item "--every-directory, -e"
List trash items moved from every directory of the (\f(CW\*(C`DIRECTORY\*(C'\fR)
filesystem. Equivalent to using \f(CW\*(C`\-\-recursive\*(C'\fR (see below) from the
mount point.
.IP "\-\-every\-filesystem, \-E" 4
.IX Item "--every-filesystem, -E"
List trash items from every directory of every known trash location. Equivalent
to using \f(CW\*(C`\-\-every\-directory\*(C'\fR at each filesystem root containing a trash
folder.  This option conflicts with an explicit \f(CW\*(C`DIRECTORY\*(C'\fR argument.
.IP "\-\-group\-by, \-G TYPE" 4
.IX Item "--group-by, -G TYPE"
Group entries by \f(CW\*(C`TYPE\*(C'\fR which is one of:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 4
day [default]
.Sp
Group entries by the day they were moved.
.IP \(bu 4
directory
.Sp
Group entries by the directory they were moved from.
.RE
.RS 4
.RE
.IP "\-\-trash\-dirs, \-T" 4
.IX Item "--trash-dirs, -T"
List trash folders instead of trash entries.
.IP "\-\-recursive, \-R" 4
.IX Item "--recursive, -R"
Recursively list entries which were moved from \f(CW\*(C`DIRECTORY\*(C'\fR and
its subdirectories.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
Trash folder information may be read from \fR\f(CI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR\fI/rmwrc\fR or
\&\fI\fR\f(CI$HOME\fR\fI/.config/rmwrc\fR
